tests: fixed /tmp file names collide across CONCURRENT runs on one host and
mask staleness via residue.

SYMPTOM (both bitten on the poseidon CI runners, 2026-07-14):
1. Several C suites hardcode /tmp names (grep '"/tmp/' tests/*.c):
   bocl_test_misc_*.tmp, bocl_cfasl_corpus.*, bocl_cfasl_feat.*, bocl_rs_test,
   bocl-test-load.lisp, bocl-test-macros.lisp, bocl-et-*, bocl-s25-*.  Three
   CI shell jobs running the suite CONCURRENTLY on one host (same user, shared
   /tmp) stomp each other's fixtures -> spurious failures.
2. Residue masks bugs: test_misc's cfasl-corpus check kept passing against a
   STALE /tmp/bocl_cfasl_corpus.fasl from July 11 for days after
   *DEFAULT-COMPILED-FILE-TYPE* changed the real output to .cfasl — the suite
   was green on the developer host and red in every clean environment (the
   docker CI images).  That expectation is fixed (v1.8.41); the residue
   MECHANISM remains for every other fixed name.

FIX SKETCH: a tests/ helper that builds per-process fixture paths
(snprintf("%s/bocl-%s-%d", getenv("TMPDIR")?:"/tmp", name, getpid())) used by
all suites, + unlink fixtures in teardown.  Until then CI routes all build
jobs to the docker executor (isolated /tmp per container), which removes the
concurrency half of the problem operationally.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FIXED (v1.8.43) — per-process fixture paths via a "{TMP}/" token.

- simple_test gained: BOCL_TEST_TMP(name) -> "$TMPDIR|/tmp"/bocl-<pid>-NAME
  (pid BEFORE the name so the file TYPE survives — compile-file derives the
  .cfasl sibling from it); BOCL_TEST_PATH(templ) expanding every "{TMP}/" in
  a string to that prefix; and BOCL_TEST_EVAL(form) = the expansion + read-
  eval, which EVERY suite's e() now routes through — a test form simply
  writes "{TMP}/fixture.lisp".  The explicit token cannot collide with a
  generated path (no double substitution) and is greppable.
- Converted all fixed fixture paths: test_misc (11 names incl. the corpus/
  feat/vm8/vm9/vm10 compile-file fixtures, C-side writers through
  BOCL_TEST_PATH, corpus/feat now deleted after use), test_slice22 (element-
  type trio + the must-not-exist probe, with delete-file cleanups),
  test_slice25 (compile-file fixtures + unlinks), test_load (suite-setup
  fixture, already unlinked in teardown), test_macros.  mkstemp users were
  already unique.  Remaining "/tmp/..." mentions are comments or
  system paths (/etc/hosts).
- VERIFIED: two test_misc processes running CONCURRENTLY both finish
  failure count = 0 (the collision case that broke the CI shell jobs);
  TMPDIR is honoured ("/custom-tmp/bocl-<pid>-x.lisp"); the fixtures are
  removed afterwards; full suite green (42 suites, failure count = 0).
